o you believe that  derek shoving should be viewed as an  exception to the rule when it comes to  policing  in my view he might not be the exception  but he's a small  minority in the minneapolis police  department you know  chief aaron dondo and i are actually  friends but i've been  abused by police and and beat up by  police and  talked back to by police but i got to  believe that most of the police in our  city  are good police officers the problem is  guys like shalvin were allowed he get 20  complaints  and still keeps his job that's a problem  no nobody else could do that and we and  the police have ignored  what we call thumpers and thumper is  somebody that arrests people and they  always get beat up  and choblin was one of those guys so  um is it a problem yes but i also say  are all black guys gang bangers no  so we have to look at the police  department department on as mayor we  need to do some changes and i think  chief aaron dondo  inherited a bunch of problems  and before him it was really crazy  what i hear when i listen to the  politicians that we have on the national  level  is a depiction of all cops as being  racist all cops as being to your word  thumpers essentially that there's no  interaction that you can have with a cop  where you can have faith that they're  going to uh you know adjudicate law and  order  not along racial lines what can we do  to replace uh sort of this type of  narrative  about cops who clearly in america you  know  the vast majority of them do a good job  they do their duty and they  they live up to the obligation that they  have to protect and serve  yeah one of the ways we have to do it is  police officers have to police  themselves  you know a fellow police officer telling  another police officer that don't do  that that is wrong  means more than me saying it you know  and  police departments have to not allow  this type of behavior  not even let the unions allow this type  of behavior  you know if you are accused of 